# Rule improvement

Update `.cursor/rules` when:

- The same pattern appears in 3+ files
- Reviews keep repeating the same feedback
- A bug class could be prevented by a short rule
- Stack or folder conventions change

Modify a rule when the codebase has a better example or the old pattern is wrong.

Quality: specific, actionable, examples from this repo, no Next.js/Expo leftovers.

New rule files follow `.cursor/rules/cursor-rules.mdc`. Remove rules that no longer match the app.
